/-!
# Presentable objects as images of small modules

Source: Hall--Neeman--Rydh, *One positive and two negative results for derived categories
of algebraic stacks*, arXiv:1405.1888v2, Remark A.4 and Lemma A.5.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-grothendieck-presentables-module-size)

The sets, module carriers, Hom sets and colimit index categories all use universe `v`.
The object universe `u` of the Grothendieck category is independent. Presentability uses
Mathlib's Hom-preservation definition, including both factorization and eventual equality.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

namespace CategoryTheory

open Limits

/-- A fixed Gabriel--Popescu presentation identifies presentable objects with images of
modules of bounded cardinality for every uncountable regular cardinal larger than the ring.
Source: Hall--Neeman--Rydh, arXiv:1405.1888v2, Remark A.4 and Lemma A.5.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-grothendieck-presentables-module-size)

Proof:
1. Choose a separator P. The separator tensor--Hom adjunction
   (`lem-sfb-separator-exact-module-adjunction`) gives R = End(P) opposite, additive
   F and G, full faithfulness of G, finite-limit preservation by F and an invertible
   counit. R is small because Hom sets are small. A left adjoint preserves small
   colimits (`lem-weil-pbc-left-adjoint-preserves-colimits`), so F is exact. Fix this
   presentation before choosing the cardinal rho.
2. For a small rho-filtered diagram x_i with colimit x, let A be the module colimit
   of G(x_i), with comparison t : A -> G(x). The colimit is the direct sum modulo
   the transition relations (`def-weil-pbc-category-colimit`). Colimit preservation
   and counit naturality identify F(A) with x and make F(t) invertible. Exactness
   kills its kernel and cokernel. A submodule generated by fewer than rho elements
   has cardinality below rho: finite lists in the union of the ring and the
   generators encode its elements (`lem-weil-pbc-finite-list-cardinality`).
3. Given small N and a map F(N) -> x with adjoint n : N -> G(x), form
   Q = N x_{G(x)} A. Its projection p to N becomes invertible under F. Choose one
   lift of each element of im(p), and let M be their generated submodule of Q.
   Then M is small, and v : M -> N has the same image as p. Its kernel embeds
   in ker(t), and its cokernel is coker(p); both are killed by F, so F(v) is
   invertible. Bounded-module presentability (`lem-sfb-small-module-cardinal-colimits`)
   factors M -> A through some G(x_i). Adjunction and inversion of F(v) factor
   the original map through x_i. This proves surjectivity of the Hom comparison.
4. If h : F(N) -> x_i vanishes in x, let n be its adjoint, z : N -> A its
   composite with the colimit map, and K = ker(z). Since F(z) = 0, exactness makes
   F(K -> N) invertible. K is small. Eventual equality for the two maps K -> G(x_i)
   given by n and zero gives i -> j annihilating n on K, since both maps agree
   in A (`lem-sfb-small-module-cardinal-colimits`). Adjunction and cancellation
   of F(K -> N) make h vanish at j. Differences handle two maps from one stage;
   filteredness moves two arbitrary stages to a common one. Thus the Hom
   comparison is injective, proving presentability of F(N) and its isomorphic objects.
5. Conversely, the submodules of G(c) of cardinality below rho form a small,
   nonempty, rho-filtered poset: regularity bounds unions of small generating sets,
   and step 2 bounds their generated sums. Cyclic submodules show their union is
   G(c); compatible maps glue uniquely, giving its module colimit. Applying F
   and the counit writes c as the colimit of the monomorphisms F(N) -> c.
   Presentability factors the identity through one such monomorphism. It is
   therefore split epic and monic, hence invertible, giving c isomorphic to F(N). -/
theorem grothendieck_presentables_module_size
    {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [Abelian C] [IsGrothendieckAbelian.{v} C] :
    ∃ (R : RingCat.{v}) (F : ModuleCat.{v} R ⥤ C) (G : C ⥤ ModuleCat.{v} R)
      (adj : F ⊣ G),
      F.Additive ∧ G.Additive ∧ G.Full ∧ G.Faithful ∧
      PreservesFiniteLimits F ∧ PreservesColimitsOfSize.{v, v} F ∧ IsIso adj.counit ∧
      ∀ (ρ : Cardinal.{v}) [Fact ρ.IsRegular],
        Cardinal.aleph0 < ρ → Cardinal.mk R < ρ →
        ∀ c : C, IsCardinalPresentable c ρ ↔
          ∃ M : ModuleCat.{v} R, Cardinal.mk M < ρ ∧ Nonempty (c ≅ F.obj M) := by
  sorry

end CategoryTheory
